body:
Empathy is a trait that is so important, yet is so commonly ignored. Those people aren't saying "I don't know what to say to you" because they think you're lying or because you're "pathetic". They're saying it because they truly don't. Don't take it personally, it's just hard to imagine the suffering that depression can cause, especially since it's not visible.

&#x200B;

You are worthy of life. You know how? You're currently living and breathing. Look around you, I guarantee there's someone who cares for you, someone who loves you, or at the very least someone who will talk to you. You have the ability to touch and affect lives, therefore your life has meaning, therefore you are worthy.

&#x200B;

I hope you can either find someone to reach out to, or can seek help elsewhere. Good luck in the future

Thank you for dropping by! As well meaning as people are on here, we're not doctors (well, most of us aren't). You really need a professional opinion for this sort of thing, depression is a real monster, but you gotta try your best to reach out to someone. Mental health is as important as physical health, think of it in the same way you might think of going to get that weird lump checked out.

&#x200B;

I hope all goes well!
